==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Kesalan Pasalan''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Ultralan Pasalan''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
This form is <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other cats from Tales of the Nekoluga, this cat is not meant to be used until it evolves.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Kesalan Pasalan is a support unit, able to stall the advance of many enemies with a knockback effect. Using and protecting him well will result in him being able to throw massive punches that send enemies flying. Do note, however, that Kesalan Pasalan is quite fragile compared to other Uber Rares and has a very long cooldown. You'll regret it if you don't protect him properly, such as with a steady stream of [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cats]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Walls]]. Kesalan Pasalan pairs very well with [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Heavy]]. Sniper can power up Kesalan Pasalan's knockback effect, allowing the two of them together to keep enemies pinned against their base (although do note that Sniper the Heavy may make Kesalan Pasalan miss).

Like all [[:Category:Cats with Knockback ability|knockback units]], it can be suicidal to use Kesalan Pasalan on some stages, as Kesalan Pasalan, despite its massive range, can unintentionally push only enemy frontliners, resulting in your other units being destroyed easily by enemy rangers. This can be the case in [[Vulcanizer (Deadly)|Vulcanizer]] and [[Unjust War (Deadly)|Unjust War]].

==='''True Form'''===
Ultralan Pasalan has an increased aggressive side, with his damage boost and freeze ability. His increased attack power lets him clear annoying peons within a very long range. His guaranteed knockback ability is very useful in [[Dark Souls (Insane)|Dark Souls]] and [[Absolute Defense (Insane)|Absolute Defence]], and when used properly, it can sometimes even knock a boss back behind their base so that you may destroy the base first and finish the stage without having to fight an overly powerful boss with a massive pool of HP. Of course, his very slow cooldown remains.

==='''Talents'''===
There isn't much to say about this unit's talents. Since this cat has a long recharge, 600¢ less cost is not going to make any difference, at least not one worth spending 175 NP on. Attack and health improvements are wasted on a unit with weak stats, while wave resistance would be nice for some stray waves, if not for the fact that Ultralan is too frail to be worth using against wave units in the first place. Freeze Up is a direct improvement, so go for that if you wish to improve this unit, just keep in mind that you would be spending a lot of NP for just one more second of freeze.

===='''Ultra Talents'''====
Ultralan Pasalan's Ultra Talents are in general surprisingly good, but what they have to offer cannot offset the extreme costs.

Given how fragile Ultralan Pasalan is, '''Surge Immunity''' does help against any surge-heavy stage, or even carry them with a proper anti-surge team. This is indeed valuable, but is mostly outclassed by the existence of various other, cheaper and more accessible alternatives. Similarly, '''Survive''' works just as well with its extreme cooldown, but requires a heavy investment to simply obtain a mediocre result.

Like any other dodge-focused unit with long cooldowns, the '''Dodge Attack''' ability is not very useful, even with a 50% activation chance when fully levelled up it only lasts for a single second. Ultralan's long cooldown and low health means as soon as enemies get to it, the unit has no hopes of getting them off easily, so it adds nothing to what it does already.

