==Trivia==
*Kesalan Pasalan gained the [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] target in [[Version 2.9.1 Update|Version 2.9.1]]. Typically this happens in the same update as the trait is introduced, but Angel was added in [[Version 2.7 Update|Version 2.7]].
*Prior to [[Version 3.4 Update|Version 3.4]], when the [[Tales of the Nekoluga (Gacha Event)|Tales of the Nekoluga]] Gacha Event was added, Nekoluga was apart of the general [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] drop pool.
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Nekoluga was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Legend of the Nekoluga (Removed Combo)|Legend of the Nekoluga]] and [[Nekoluganomicon (Removed Combo)|Nekoluganomicon]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Nekoluga's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Nekoluga
Not sure if this is a Cat…
Maybe if you evolve him…</pre>
<pre>Unknown Cat
God, I don't know if this is a Cat anymore.
Seriously, I give up.
Knocks back enemies. (Area Atk.)</pre>
<pre>Ultralan Pasalan
Tired of scaring children, Luga decided to reinvent
himself as that famous masked hero. Freezes
and knocks back non-Metal enemies (Area Atk.)</pre>
*The word "neko" is Japanese for "cat". The reason that Nekoluga has this name is probably due to the fact that he is the mascot of all Nekolugas.
*Kesalan Pasalan is named after the Japanese cryptid [[wikipedia:ja:ケサランパサラン|Kesaran Pasaran]], a mysterious, white ball of fluff that is said to bring good luck.
*Prior to Version 15.7, Kesalan Pasalan was named Unknown Cat, making him the only evolved Luga to not follow the naming scheme of the others (''[prefix]''lan Pasalan). This was only the case in [[BCEN]], as his Japanese name has always been ケサランパサラン (''Kesaran Pasaran'').
**The name Kesalan Pasalan was used in English during the [[PONOS Campaigns/The Great Nyanko Tournament|Great Nyanko Tournament]] and in [[The Battle Cats Unite!]] years before he was renamed in the mobile version.
*According to his design, name and description, Ultralan Pasalan is a reference to a kid-loved Japanese fictional gigantic masked hero, [[wikipedia:Ultraman|Ultraman]]. His large horns also reference [[wikia:ultra:Father of Ultra|Father of Ultra]].
**If observed closely, Ultralan Pasalan's "heart" glows red when he is knocked back or killed, just like how Ultraman's "heart" also glows red when his energy is running out.
*Nekoluga was the first Uber Rare Cat added to the game and was also the first unit to have a guaranteed effect, Knockback in his case.
*Ultralan Pasalan and [[Mola King (Uber Rare Cat)|Master of the Pacific]] are the only units with Dodge Attack [[Talents]] that increases the effect's chance instead of its duration.
**Strangely enough, Ultralan Pasalan's Talent description is 'Unlocks the "Dodge" ability. Level up to increase the length of Dodge effects!' despite it being the chance that is upgraded. This description is exactly the same as units who have their length extended, so it is likely just a copy-and-paste error.
*Nekoluga and [[Togeluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Togeluga]] are the only two units to have their gender shown in the banner tab.
*Nekoluga and [[Balaluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Balaluga]] are currently the only Lugas to have a seasonal variant, those being [[Summerluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Summerluga]] and [[Betrothed Balaluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Betrothed Balaluga]].
*In [[The Battle Cats Unite!]], Nekoluga's description is replaced with that of [[Asiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Asiluga]]'s Normal Form.

